			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>The only actors I can remember that played superheros on film and aren't clearly recognizable with their masks on are the ones that played Spider-Man. </p><p>About the turtles: the only purpose they seem to have is allow people to distinguish one turtle from the other. Because armbands and weapons are not enough in close shots.</p><p>Or maybe turtles distinguish themselves only by the skin around their eyes. That must be it. I wonder how rats work.</p>",
